## HTML attachment preview for Confluence Server / Data Center 6.9+
##
## Admin setup:
##   1. Management → User Macros → Create User Macro
##   2. Macro name: confluence-html-previewer
##   3. Visibility: Visible to all users
##   4. Macro Title: confluence-html-previewer
##      The macro browser lists and searches this title, not the macro name alone.
##   5. Categories: pick at least one, for example Development
##   6. Macro body: Has body
##   7. Body processing: Rendered
##   8. Output: HTML
##   9. Paste this template into the User Macro only (not Custom HTML)
##  10. Icon URL: the hosted dist/html-previewer.icon.png
##  11. Custom HTML → At end of the BODY:
##        <script src=".../html-previewer.init.js"></script>
##
## Authors insert one or more HTML attachments in the macro body, as a
## link or a thumbnail. The view page shows each file on its own row.
## Do not put <script> tags in this template.
##
## @noparams is required. Without @param or @noparams, the macro browser
## omits the macro.

## @noparams

<div class="confluence-html-previewer" data-state="pending">
$body
</div>
